# Append-only cross-LLM log: every branch prepends a new entry at the top, so two
# branches collide at the same spot on every merge. `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides'
# added lines (no conflict markers) instead of failing. Safe here because entries are
# added as new blocks, never by editing existing lines.
# Do NOT extend this to docs/system_risk_register.md — it has in-place Status edits
# that a union merge would silently corrupt; leave it on the normal 3-way merge.
docs/SESSION_LOG.md merge=union

# Sha256-pinned entry-funnel calibration fixtures: byte-exact, no EOL conversion,
# so the preregistration's frozen sha matches on every checkout regardless of
# core.autocrlf (otherwise Windows CRLF-smudge drifts the sha and the calibration
# test skips its frozen-replay assertions).
tests/fixtures/a_short_entry_funnel_calibration/*.json -text

# Same class, different artifact: the comparison ledgers record the RAW sha256 of
# published weekly bundles (`m67_provenance.source_sha256`, the official-operation
# capture's source identity). With core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone/worktree
# smudges these to CRLF, the recorded sha stops matching, and the source-binding
# assertions fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the code under review.
research/results/a_short/**/weekly_m67.json -text
research/results/a_short/**/weekly_m67.receipt.json -text
research/results/a_short/**/weekly_m67.md -text
